# Sakhi server — environment
# Copy to .env (or export these) and fill in what you need. Everything here is
# optional: with no keys at all the app still runs, using rules-only triage.
# That is a real degraded mode, not a broken one.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Triage reasoning (IBM watsonx.ai Granite)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Without these the rules engine runs alone. The model can only ever RAISE the
# urgency the rules produced, never lower it.
WATSONX_API_KEY=
WATSONX_PROJECT_ID=
# WATSONX_URL=https://us-south.ml.cloud.ibm.com

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Session storage (Supabase Postgres)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Leave both blank and sessions are kept in server/data/sessions.json. That is
# the zero-config demo path and it works — but Render's disk is ephemeral, so a
# restart loses the triage queue. Set these for any real deployment.
#
# Setup: create a project at supabase.com, then run migrations/001_schema.sql in
# the SQL editor. Both variables are required together; a URL without a key
# falls back to the JSON file and logs a warning at boot.
SUPABASE_URL=
# Project Settings -> API -> service_role. This key bypasses Row Level Security
# and is the only credential that can read the session table, so it is
# server-only: never put it in client/.env, never prefix it with VITE_, and
# rotate it if it is ever committed. The anon key is not used here — the browser
# never talks to Supabase directly.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Server
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PORT=4000
# ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173,http://127.0.0.1:5173
# Set only when running behind a reverse proxy you control, so that
# X-Forwarded-For can be trusted for rate limiting.
# TRUST_PROXY=false

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Demo accounts (development only)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Password used by `npm run seed:demo`.
# DEMO_PASSWORD=SakhiDemo@2026!
